  { q: 'What is the story of Raven stealing the sun?', a: 'In the most widespread version of the Raven creation cycle, Raven discovers that a powerful chief or old man keeps the sun, moon, and stars locked in boxes in his house. Raven, unable to reach them directly, transforms himself into a spruce needle (or salmon egg) that the chief\'s daughter swallows, is born as her child, and gradually wins the boxes as toys. He then escapes through the smoke-hole, releasing the sun, moon, and stars into the sky for all humanity. The story explains both the origin of celestial light and Raven\'s characteristic black colour — he was scorched in the escape.' },
